    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d887">

                <pb facs="1052" n="1036" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg1036"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2331/5–947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Peru </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-05-19T15:00:00-04:00">May 19, 1947—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>247. Embs 346 May 9. In view stock position Peru, Dept Agri has told Peruvians
                    they are now permitted buy 10,000 tons flour for as early shipment as can be
                    arranged. Peruvian Emb says flour acceptable. Most other countries taking a far
                    larger percent of imports in form of flour than is Peru.</p>
                <p>US July export program just announced includes 8,500 tons wheat for Peru.</p>
                <p>It is hoped that these emergency allocations will improve Peru’s bargaining
                    position in its current negotiations with Argentina.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
